Overlay patch 0048: VR culling gate — view-direction culling stands down,
distance culling stays (VR-spec D5, trap A2).

RaYRoD's MK64-VR changelog is explicit about the shape of this fix and the
cost of getting it wrong: killing ALL culling (his patch 6) stopped scenery
vanishing but "every race began over budget & dragged", so patch 7 put the
distance cull back and relaxed only the direction cull. The headset's FOV is
much wider than the chase camera's frustum — and in VR the head can look
anywhere, including behind — so the yaw cone is simply the wrong test; the
distance test is still exactly right and is what keeps the frame budget.

is_within_render_distance is the single chokepoint: every one of the port's
~25 cull sites (including the Moo Moo Farm cow site 0033 guards) funnels
through it, and the distance rejections all happen BEFORE the angle test.
Widening the cone to a full circle in VR world frames therefore relaxes
direction and nothing else.

0xB6 * fov * scaleFov is the half-cone in u16 binary angles; 0x7FFF is one
LSB short of half a revolution, so plus/minus covers the whole circle
without wrapping onto itself (0x8000 would make the two bounds equal).

Deliberately anchored on the plus/minus angle computation rather than on
scaleFov: overlay 0032 edits the scaleFov block a dozen lines up, and a
patch whose context overlaps another patch's inserted text breaks that
patch's reverse probe in apply-overlay.sh (R0's structural finding).
Gated on gSohVRWorldActive, so flat and 3D-panel builds are untouched.


--- a/src/racing/math_util.c
+++ b/src/racing/math_util.c
@@ -1152,6 +1152,20 @@
     }
 
     angleObject = get_angle_between_two_vectors(cameraPos, objectPos);
+#ifdef __IOS__
+    // SOH_IOS (overlay 0048): VR culling gate (VR-spec D5 / trap A2).
+    // In VR world frames the head owns the view and can look anywhere the
+    // chase camera never pointed, so the yaw cone is the wrong test — stand
+    // it down to a full circle. Every distance rejection above this line
+    // still runs, which is the half of the cull that owns the frame budget
+    // (RaYRoD's patch 6 killed both and "every race began over budget").
+    {
+        extern volatile int gSohVRWorldActive;
+        if (gSohVRWorldActive) {
+            extended_fov = 32767.0f; // one LSB short of half a revolution
+        }
+    }
+#endif
     minus_fov_angle = (s32)orientationY - (s32)extended_fov;
     plus_fov_angle = (s32)orientationY + (s32)extended_fov;
 
